1
00:00:04,439 --> 00:00:08,039
Chapter 25.

2
00:00:10,198 --> 00:00:16,560
Men," said the little prince, "set out on their way in express trains,

3
00:00:16,560 --> 00:00:19,679
but they do not know what they are looking for.

4
00:00:19,679 --> 00:00:25,139
Then they rush about, and get excited, and turn round and round..."

5
00:00:25,139 --> 00:00:30,800
And he added: "It is not worth the trouble..."

6
00:00:31,020 --> 00:00:35,579
The world that we had come to was not like the wells of the Sahara.

7
00:00:35,579 --> 00:00:39,779
The wells of the Sahara are mere holes dug in the sand.

8
00:00:39,779 --> 00:00:42,899
This one was like a well in a village.

9
00:00:42,899 --> 00:00:49,279
But there was no village here, and I thought I must be dreaming...

10
00:00:49,560 --> 00:00:54,539
"It is strange," I said the little prince.

11
00:00:54,539 --> 00:01:01,198
"Everything is ready for use: the pulley, the bucket, the rope..."

12
00:01:01,198 --> 00:01:05,819
He laughed, touched the rope, and set the pulley to working.

13
00:01:05,819 --> 00:01:13,099
And the pulley moaned, like an old Weather Vein which the wind has long since forgotten.

14
00:01:13,139 --> 00:01:16,679
"Do you hear the little prince.

15
00:01:16,679 --> 00:01:21,238
"We have awakened the well, and it is singing..."

16
00:01:21,238 --> 00:01:24,658
I did not want him to tire himself with the rope.

17
00:01:24,658 --> 00:01:27,420
"Leave it to me," I said.

18
00:01:27,420 --> 00:01:30,800
"It is too heavy for you."

19
00:01:31,679 --> 00:01:36,479
I hoisted the bucket slowly to the edge of the well and set it there--

20
00:01:36,479 --> 00:01:42,179
happy, tired as I was, over my achievement.

21
00:01:42,179 --> 00:01:47,340
The song of the pulley was still in my ears, and I could see the sunlight shimmer in

22
00:01:47,340 --> 00:01:50,599
the still trembling water.

23
00:01:51,599 --> 00:01:56,880
"I am thirsty for this water," said the little prince.

24
00:01:56,880 --> 00:02:00,238
"Give me some of it to drink..."

25
00:02:00,238 --> 00:02:04,500
And then I understood what he had been looking for.

26
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:07,079
I raised the bucket to his lips.

27
00:02:07,079 --> 00:02:11,639
He drank, his eyes closed.

28
00:02:11,639 --> 00:02:16,380
It was as sweet as some special festival treat.

29
00:02:16,380 --> 00:02:20,939
This water was indeed a different thing from ordinary nourishment.

30
00:02:20,939 --> 00:02:26,520
Its sweetness was born of the walk under the stars, the song of the pulley the

31
00:02:26,520 --> 00:02:29,039
effort in my arms.

32
00:02:29,039 --> 00:02:34,880
It was good for the heart, like a present.

33
00:02:35,340 --> 00:02:40,198
When I was a little boy, the lights of the Christmas tree, the music of the

34
00:02:40,198 --> 00:02:46,319
Midnight Mass, the tenderness of smiling faces, used to make up, so,

35
00:02:46,319 --> 00:02:51,679
the radiance of the gifts I received.

36
00:02:52,020 --> 00:02:59,520
"The men where you live," said the little prince, "raise 5 000 roses in the same garden--

37
00:02:59,520 --> 00:03:04,198
and they do not find in it what they are looking for."

38
00:03:04,198 --> 00:03:08,639
"They do not find it," I replied.

39
00:03:08,639 --> 00:03:13,500
"And yet what they are looking for could be found in one single rose

40
00:03:13,500 --> 00:03:17,039
boring just a little water."

41
00:03:17,039 --> 00:03:22,679
"Yes, that is true," I said.

42
00:03:22,679 --> 00:03:28,260
And a little prince added: "But the eyes are blind.

43
00:03:28,260 --> 00:03:32,658
One must look with the heart..."

44
00:03:32,760 --> 00:03:35,219
I had drunk the water.

45
00:03:35,219 --> 00:03:37,979
I breathed easily.

46
00:03:37,979 --> 00:03:42,060
At sunrise the sand is the color of honey.

47
00:03:42,060 --> 00:03:46,319
And that honey color was making me happy, too.

48
00:03:46,319 --> 00:03:52,520
What brought me, then, this sense of grief?

49
00:03:53,219 --> 00:03:58,139
"You must keep your promise," said the little prince, softly, as he sat

50
00:03:58,139 --> 00:04:01,500
down beside me once more.

51
00:04:01,500 --> 00:04:04,880
"What promise

52
00:04:06,060 --> 00:04:09,060
a muscle for my sheep...

53
00:04:09,060 --> 00:04:13,939
I am responsible for this flower..."

54
00:04:14,340 --> 00:04:18,238
I took my rough drafts of drawings out of my pocket.

55
00:04:18,238 --> 00:04:25,859
The little prince looked them over, and left as he said: "Your baobabs-- they look a little like

56
00:04:25,859 --> 00:04:27,840
cabbages."

57
00:04:27,840 --> 00:04:29,760
"Oh!"

58
00:04:29,760 --> 00:04:33,539
I had been so proud of my baobabs!

59
00:04:33,539 --> 00:04:40,800
"Your fox-- his ears look a little like horns; and they are too long."

60
00:04:40,800 --> 00:04:43,500
And he laughed again.

61
00:04:43,500 --> 00:04:47,399
"You are not fair, little prince," I said.

62
00:04:47,399 --> 00:04:51,658
"I don't know how to draw anything except boa constrictors from the outside and

63
00:04:51,658 --> 00:04:55,020
boa constrictors from the inside."

64
00:04:55,020 --> 00:05:02,539
"Oh, that will be all right," he said, "children understand."

65
00:05:03,118 --> 00:05:06,479
So then I made a pencil sketch of a muzzle.

66
00:05:06,479 --> 00:05:12,020
And I gave it to him my heart was torn.

67
00:05:12,479 --> 00:05:18,658
"You have plans that I don't know about," I said.

68
00:05:18,658 --> 00:05:21,359
But he did not answer me.

69
00:05:21,359 --> 00:05:29,420
He said to me, instead: "You know-- my descent to the earth...

70
00:05:29,639 --> 00:05:34,260
Tomorrow will be its anniversary."

71
00:05:34,260 --> 00:05:39,560
Then, after a silence, he went on:

72
00:05:40,618 --> 00:05:44,279
"I came down very near here."

73
00:05:44,279 --> 00:05:46,859
And he flushed.

74
00:05:46,859 --> 00:05:53,279
And once again, without understanding why, I had a queer sense of sorrow.

75
00:05:53,279 --> 00:06:00,719
One question, however, occurred to me: "Then it was not by chance that on the

76
00:06:00,719 --> 00:06:05,158
morning when I first met you-- a week ago-- you were strolling along like that, all

77
00:06:05,158 --> 00:06:08,760
alone, a thousand miles from an inhabited region?

78
00:06:08,760 --> 00:06:13,738
You were on your way back to the place where you landed?"

79
00:06:13,738 --> 00:06:16,979
The little prince flushed again.

80
00:06:16,979 --> 00:06:21,560
And I added, with some hesitancy:

81
00:06:22,139 --> 00:06:27,079
"Perhaps it was because of the anniversary?"

82
00:06:27,118 --> 00:06:30,539
The little prince flushed once more.

83
00:06:30,539 --> 00:06:40,219
He never answered questions-- but when one flushes does that not mean "Yes"?

84
00:06:41,158 --> 00:06:51,060
"Ah," I said to him, "I think I'm a little frightened--" But he interrupted me.

85
00:06:51,060 --> 00:06:57,479
"Now you must work. You must return to your engine. I will be waiting for you here.

86
00:06:57,479 --> 00:07:01,020
Come back tomorrow evening..."

87
00:07:01,020 --> 00:07:03,899
But I was not reassured.

88
00:07:03,899 --> 00:07:07,460
I remembered the fox.

89
00:07:07,679 --> 00:07:16,579
One runs the risk of weeping a little, if one lets himself be tamed
